<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ireland's Waterford Wedgwood says profits rose 24 percent.</title>
<headline>Ireland's Waterford Wedgwood says profits rose 24 percent.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN, Ireland</dateline>
<text>
<p>Waterford Wedgwood Plc, which makes crystal, fine china and ceramics, said Monday that its pre-tax profits rose 24 percent to 34.9 million Irish pounds ($54.7 million) on sales of 376.3 million ($590.7 million).</p>
</text>
